# Byte-pinned shipped references -------------------------------------------------
# R/refdb.R verifies sha256 digests over the EXACT shipped bytes (fail-closed).
# Windows runners check out with core.autocrlf=true; without these `-text`
# pins the .txt matrices are silently CRLF-rewritten and every refdb and
# benchmark-driver test dies on a digest mismatch (CI audit 2026-10-07:
# expected 282126c3..., got d2d4c473... == LF->CRLF rehash of
# COSMIC_v3.6_SBS_GRCh37.txt). The .rds manifest is binary but shares the
# same bundle and the same byte-pinning discipline.
inst/reference/** -text

# Byte-pinned test fixtures ----------------------------------------------------
# test-catalog-currency.R compares the golden downloads page against the
# helper-generated page byte for byte (writeBin/readBin raw bytes); with
# core.autocrlf=true Windows checkouts the html arrived CRLF-rewritten and
# the unit died on per-line \r deltas (PR #26 CI audit 2026-10-14:
# windows-latest/R-release testthat failure at test-catalog-currency.R:504,
# all other arms green). The .txt specimen
# shares the same hazard family. Pin the whole fixtures tree to raw bytes,
# same discipline as the refdb pins above.
tests/testthat/fixtures/** -text

# Byte-pinned one-shot gate evidence ------------------------------------------------
# tools/kl-gate-p1/result.md and data/outputs/ are the machine-written
# attestation audited by test-kernel-gate-evidence.R (anchored row regexes
# `^|...` and byte-comparisons against the kernel-cli goldens). The same
# core.autocrlf=true CRLF-rewrite hazard as the fixtures above (PR #26
# law): an unpinned Windows checkout would inject per-line \r and turn a
# green record mechanically red. Pin the whole tool dir to raw bytes.
tools/kl-gate-p1/** -text
